{#
settings/_calendars.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Calendar management: create, rename, recolour, re-zone, show/hide, choose where
new events land, delete.

One flat list in sort order. Which calendar a row is — the user's own, a mail
account's, one they made — is a badge rather than a section, because the
actions available differ per row and grouping them would say the same thing
twice.

Three rules are rendered, not just enforced (CalendarSettingsController holds
the server side of each):

  A provisioned calendar has no delete button. CalendarRole::isDeletable()
  decides, and the answer is no for the personal one and for an account's,
  because deleting either only means the provisioner makes it again.

  The default has no delete button and no hide button. It is where a new event
  lands, so removing it or hiding it makes new events vanish on save.

  Everything can be renamed, including an account's calendar — which is the
  point, since those are provisioned named after a username.

A fourth rule arrived with subscribing, and it is the reason the row grew a
second line: a mirrored calendar is the only kind that can be *silently broken*.
It syncs on a sweep nobody watches, so where it comes from, whether it accepts
writes, when it last worked and why it stopped are rendered on the row — every
one of them a fact the user cannot find anywhere else. A row that mirrors
nothing renders exactly as it did before, with no second line at all.

Variables:
  calendars            Calendar[]     every calendar the user owns, in sort order
  calendarAccounts     Account[]      accounts calendars can be subscribed from
  calendarConnections  Integration[]  CalDAV connections calendars can be subscribed from
#}
{% include 'settings/_calendar_sources.html.twig' with {
    calendarAccounts: calendarAccounts|default([]),
    calendarConnections: calendarConnections|default([]),
} only %}

<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3 border-b border-line bg-sunken">
    <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'settings.calendars.count'|trans({ '%count%': calendars|length }) }}</p>

    <button
        data-controller="ui--modal"
        data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.form.add'|trans }}"
        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_new') }}"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-white transition-colors cursor-pointer"
    >
        <i class="fa-solid fa-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {{ 'calendar.form.add'|trans }}
    </button>
</div>

{% if calendars is empty %}
    <p class="px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
        {{ 'settings.calendars.empty'|trans }}
    </p>
{% else %}
    <ul class="py-2 divide-y divide-line">
        {% for calendar in calendars %}
            {# `isSynced` and not `role`: a Remote calendar the subscribe flow
               created but never bound to a remote id mirrors nothing, and
               offering it a "sync now" button would queue a job the handler
               refuses. Calendar::isSynced() is the one place that decides. #}
            {% set mirrors = calendar.isSynced %}
            {% set origin = calendar.integration ? calendar.integration.name
                          : (calendar.account ? calendar.account.displayAddress : null) %}

            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-1.5">

                <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full shrink-0"
                      style="background-color: {{ calendar.color }}"
                      aria-hidden="true"></span>

                <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-0.5">
                    <span class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
                        <span class="truncate text-sm {{ calendar.isVisible ? 'text-ink' : 'text-ink-faint' }}">
                            {{ calendar.name }}
                        </span>

                        {% if calendar.isDefault %}
                            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-accent/10 text-accent">
                                {{ 'settings.calendars.default'|trans }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}

                        {% if mirrors %}
                            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-accent/10 text-accent"
                                  title="{{ 'settings.calendars.mirrored_hint'|trans({ '%name%': origin }) }}">
                                {{ 'settings.calendars.mirrored'|trans }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}

                        {% if calendar.isReadOnly %}
                            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-zinc-500/10 text-ink-muted"
                                  title="{{ 'settings.calendars.read_only_hint'|trans }}">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock mr-1 text-[8px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                {{ 'settings.calendars.read_only'|trans }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}

                        {% if calendar.account and not mirrors %}
                            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-zinc-500/10 text-ink-muted"
                                  title="{{ 'settings.calendars.account_hint'|trans({ '%address%': calendar.account.displayAddress }) }}">
                                {{ calendar.account.displayAddress }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}

                        <span class="text-[10px] text-ink-faint">{{ calendar.timeZone }}</span>
                    </span>

                    {# Only for a calendar that mirrors something. A local list
                       has no remote to have last spoken to, and a "never
                       synced" line under every hand-made calendar would teach
                       people to stop reading the one that matters. #}
                    {% if mirrors %}
                        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 min-w-0 text-[10px] text-ink-faint">
                            <span class="truncate">{{ 'settings.calendars.from'|trans({ '%name%': origin }) }}</span>
                            <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                            {% if calendar.lastSyncedAt %}
                                <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'settings.calendars.last_synced'|trans({ '%when%': calendar.lastSyncedAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }) }}</span>
                            {% else %}
                                <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'settings.calendars.never_synced'|trans }}</span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </span>

                        {# lastSyncError is written for display and never
                           carries a credential — see Calendar::$lastSyncError.
                           Shown in full rather than truncated to a chip,
                           because it is the whole reason a calendar is empty. #}
                        {% if calendar.lastSyncError %}
                            <span role="alert" class="flex items-start gap-1.5 text-[10px] text-danger leading-snug">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-px shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span>{{ calendar.lastSyncError }}</span>
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% endif %}
                </span>

                <div class="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0">
                    {% if mirrors %}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_sync', { id: calendar.id }) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-sync' ~ calendar.id) }}">
                            <button
                                type="submit"
                                class="w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-accent hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                                aria-label="{{ 'settings.calendars.sync_now'|trans({ '%name%': calendar.name }) }}"
                                title="{{ 'settings.calendars.sync_now_title'|trans }}"
                            >
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </button>
                        </form>
                    {% endif %}

                    {% if not calendar.isDefault %}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_make_default', { id: calendar.id }) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-default' ~ calendar.id) }}">
                            <button
                                type="submit"
                                class="w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-accent hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                                aria-label="{{ 'settings.calendars.make_default'|trans({ '%name%': calendar.name }) }}"
                                title="{{ 'settings.calendars.make_default_title'|trans }}"
                            >
                                <i class="fa-regular fa-star text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </button>
                        </form>
                    {% endif %}

                    <button
                        data-controller="ui--modal"
                        data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.form.edit'|trans }}"
                        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_edit', { id: calendar.id }) }}"
                        class="w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-ink hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                        aria-label="{{ 'settings.calendars.edit'|trans({ '%name%': calendar.name }) }}"
                        title="{{ 'calendar.form.edit'|trans }}"
                    >
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-pen text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>

                    {% if calendar.role.isDeletable and not calendar.isDefault %}
                        {# The confirmation says the events go too, because they
                           do — the join column cascades — and there is no way to
                           empty a calendar first. #}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_delete', { id: calendar.id }) }}"
                              data-turbo-confirm="{{ 'calendar.delete_confirm'|trans({ '%name%': calendar.name }) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-delete' ~ calendar.id) }}">
                            <button
                                type="submit"
                                class="w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-danger hover:bg-danger-soft transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                                aria-label="{{ 'settings.calendars.delete'|trans({ '%name%': calendar.name }) }}"
                                title="{{ 'settings.calendars.delete_title'|trans }}"
                            >
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-trash text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </button>
                        </form>
                    {% endif %}

                    {% if not calendar.isDefault or not calendar.isVisible %}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_toggle_visibility', { id: calendar.id }) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-visibility' ~ calendar.id) }}">
                            <button
                                type="submit"
                                class="w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-ink hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                                aria-label="{{ calendar.isVisible ? 'settings.calendars.hide'|trans : 'settings.calendars.show'|trans }}"
                                title="{{ calendar.isVisible ? 'settings.calendars.hide'|trans : 'settings.calendars.show'|trans }}"
                            >
                                <i class="fa-solid {{ calendar.isVisible ? 'fa-eye text-accent' : 'fa-eye-slash' }} text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </button>
                        </form>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% endif %}
